# Trivy vulnerability allowlist for released container images.
# Used by .github/workflows/release.yml's image-scan step.
#
# Add an entry only for a CVE that's been triaged and judged not exploitable
# in this image's context (e.g. affected code path is unused). One CVE ID
# per line, with a comment explaining why it's suppressed and a date so
# stale entries can be revisited.
#
# Example:
# CVE-2024-00000 # not reachable — affected codepath unused in this image, reviewed 2026-08-02

CVE-2026-14257 # ReDoS in brace-expansion bundled inside npm's own CLI (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm), not our app's dependency tree; runtime only runs `npx prisma migrate deploy` and `node dist/server.js`, never npm glob/pattern matching on untrusted input. Fixed version (5.0.8) isn't in any published npm release yet — revisit and drop this entry once npm ships one that bundles it. Reviewed 2026-08-03.
CVE-2026-69152 # ReDoS in brace-expansion, again vendored inside npm's own global CLI install (verified: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion, version 5.0.7 — the npm CLI binary itself, not our workspace's dependency tree, which already resolves brace-expansion at fixed versions per package-lock.json). web's runtime command is `npx next start`, which execs the already-installed local `next` binary directly (verified present at apps/web/node_modules/.bin/next) — npx never touches the registry or npm's own glob-matching code path here. Fixed version 5.0.9 exists upstream but npm@latest (12.0.2 at build time) hasn't picked it up into its own vendored copy yet. Reviewed 2026-08-05.
CVE-2026-69192 # ip-address vulnerability, same situation — vendored inside npm's own global CLI (used internally by npm's bundled `socks` package for SOCKS-proxy support), not our dependency tree. Only reachable if npm itself makes a registry/network call through a SOCKS proxy, which never happens at web's container runtime (`npx next start` execs an already-installed local binary — see CVE-2026-69152 above). Fixed version 10.3.1 exists upstream but npm@latest (12.0.2) hasn't picked it up yet. Reviewed 2026-08-05.
